<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Quaestor</title>
<meta name="description" content="A multi-tenant AR/AP ledger that observes, records, and proves — and never moves money.">
<style is:global>
  :root { --accent: #7c3aed; --bg: #fafaf9; --fg: #1c1917; --muted: #57534e; --card: #ffffff; --border: #e7e5e4; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg: #0c0a09; --fg: #fafaf9; --muted: #a8a29e; --card: #1c1917; --border: #292524; }
  }
  * { margin: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.6 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
  header, main, footer { max-width: 60rem; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: 1.5rem; }
  header { padding-top: 4rem; }
  .latin { color: var(--accent); font-style: italic; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .tagline { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 44rem; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 3rem 0; }
  .card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 0.75rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; }
  .card h2 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .card p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .rule { height: 3px; width: 4rem; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 2px; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; } a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="latin">quaestor — the magistrate who kept Rome&#39;s accounts</div>
  <h1>Quaestor</h1>
  <p class="tagline">A multi-tenant AR/AP ledger that observes, records, and proves — and never moves money.</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>
</header>
<main>
  <div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h2>Append-only ledger</h2><p>Double-entry postings that must sum to zero per currency, enforced in Postgres by triggers — UPDATE and DELETE are forbidden.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Observer posture</h2><p>Reads, ledgers, and reconciles across Stripe, PayPal, Braintree, Plaid, and banks — never moves money on its own license.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>On-chain tamper evidence</h2><p>Periodic Merkle-root anchoring to Solana with an independent third-party verification endpoint.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Read-only crypto</h2><p>Watches Solana and EVM wallets into the same per-entity ledger as fiat. No keys, no spend authority.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Multi-tenant by design</h2><p>Every row carries a shard key derived from tenant and regulatory region.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Two answers, fast</h2><p>When do I bill the customer, and when do I pay the vendor — one GET each.</p></div>
  </div>
</main>
<footer>
  <a href="https://github.com/quaestor-ledger">GitHub org</a>
  <a href="https://github.com/quaestor-ledger/billing-server.rs">Server repository</a>
  <span>© 2026 Quaestor</span>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
